  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only result is config_006 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) at 0.653 acc / 0.628 F1, with config_005 (avgpool) nearly identical at 0.650. Image-only resnet50 is very weak (0.208), raising the question of whether adding image features to a strong RNA pipeline helps or hurts. Question: Does multimodal fusion (concat) of resnet50 image features with the best RNA pipeline (scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer) improve validation accuracy over the RNA-only baseline? This is the most direct, single-variable extension of our best result—adding only the image modality via concat fusion while keeping all other RNA-side choices identical to config_006. Why this is the best use of experiment 8: With only 2 experiments left, we need to determine whether the multimodal direction is worth pursuing at all. If concat fusion with resnet50 shows no gain (or a loss), we can rule out the simpler multimodal path and focus remaining budget on confirming the RNA-only optimum. If it shows a gain, the final experiment can test weighted fusion or ViT-L to squeeze out further improvement. This cleanly isolates the fusion effect without confounding with a new image encoder."
}

